        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add plan-first Claw status and remove",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add experimental `claws status [claw-or-agent]` across canonical agent, workspace, package, session, and scheduled-job state\n- bind every remove choice and observed owner/dependency edge into an exact dry-run `planIntegrity` digest\n- classify resources consistently as `managed` or `referenced`, with separate origin and current non-Claw owner evidence\n- retain referenced resources by default, support safe `--remove-unused`, and support exact repeatable `--remove-referenced <kind:ref@version>` selection\n- require `--force-referenced` when a selected resource has another Claw dependent, a non-Claw owner, or pre-existing origin\n- invoke canonical skill/plugin removal only after revalidation under the shared cross-process package lifecycle lease\n\n## Scope\n\nThis is the authoritative status/remove slice for the experimental one-Claw/one-agent contract. Root and orphaned subordinate provenance are inventoried so missing root rows do not hide recoverable package or workspace state.\n\nRemove is plan-first. Dry-run includes agent identity, config-removal surfaces, bindings, allow entries, scheduled-job blockers, managed-file digests, package relationship/origin/integrity, every known affected Claw, current non-Claw ownership, cleanup mode, filesystem targets, and root state. Apply requires `--yes --plan-integrity <digest>`, rebuilds the same plan with the same cleanup mode, and fails closed on drift.\n\nManaged resources are cleaned by default when ownership and content are still provable. Referenced resources default to retain/release. `--remove-unused` selects only complete, unchanged, unambiguous, Claw-introduced resources with no other Claw edge or non-Claw owner. `--remove-referenced` selects exact resources; conflicts require the separate `--force-referenced` acknowledgement and remain visible in the plan. A general `--yes` never broadens cleanup.\n\nOrdinary OpenClaw behavior is unchanged. Direct package operations record current independent ownership, ordinary uninstall remains authoritative after Claw-reference warnings, and Claw removal delegates actual mutation to canonical package owners. No refcount or permanent removal tombstone is introduced. Everything remains behind `OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1`.\n\n## Stack\n\n- RFC: https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/27\n- Depends on: #102228 package lifecycle and provenance\n- This PR: status, exact remove planning, cleanup choices, canonical removal, and recovery\n- Next: #102306 export\n\n## Validation\n\nExact head: `f683f60b0fb`.\n\n- Node 24.15.0 / SQLite 3.51.3: 47 package/lifecycle/adoption unit tests passed\n- Node 24.15.0 / SQLite 3.51.3: 21 Claws CLI tests passed\n- focused tests cover default retention, remove-if-unused, exact selected cleanup, conflict override, canonical plugin uninstall, direct-owner adoption, orphan inventory, and digest-bound apply\n- scoped Oxfmt and Oxlint passed on all changed files\n- GitHub `check-test-types`, `check-prod-types`, max-lines, security, and focused matrix checks pass; final CI is rerunning after two quality-gate fixes\n- `git diff --check` passed\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nThe lifecycle E2E invokes the real CLI in isolated state and proves `add -> status -> remove --dry-run -> --yes --plan-integrity` with canonical agent and managed workspace cleanup. Focused exact-head tests additionally execute the canonical plugin-uninstall dependency for selected referenced cleanup and verify that default removal only releases the Claw edge.",
